-- Companion to aggregate_taking_container, guarding the limits of when the
-- attribute filters of an aggregate may use attributes that only some of the
-- possible contents of a container have.
--
-- The relaxation rests entirely on the existance filter that is generated
-- before the filters for arithmetic aggregates, so it only holds where that
-- filter is generated, and only for the class it tests for. Both aggregates
-- below must therefore still be reported as error 316.

The room Isa location
End the.

The hero Isa actor At room
  Is total 0.
End the.

The closet Isa entity
  Container Taking garment.
End the.

Every garment Isa thing
  Is cover 0.
  Is washed.
  Container Taking gadget.
End every.

Every gadget Isa thing
  Is charged.
End every.

Verb probe
  Does
    -- COUNT has no attribute to aggregate over, so no existance filter is
    -- generated and nothing has been skipped when the filters are applied.
    Set total Of hero To Count Is washed, In closet.

    -- Here the existance filter skips everything that is not a garment, so
    -- 'charged', which only the gadgets have, is still not available.
    Set total Of hero To Sum Of cover Is charged, In closet.
End verb.

Start At room.
